:: Church {"position":"700,500","size":"100,100"}
You press on toward the towering church at the center of the city. The massive doors hang slightly ajar, and the scent of rot grows stronger with each step. You know the creature is inside.

Before you reach the door, a low, guttural growl freezes you in place.

The monster emerges, hunched and bristling with unnatural rage. Its voice, a rasp of human words twisted by its transformation, chills you to the bone: "You will die here."

In its yellowed eyes, you see a flicker of humanity-a soul begging to be freed. 

You draw your weapon.


[move Battle]


:: Churchyard {"position":"500,500","size":"100,100"}
The streets gradually widen into a neglected square where cracked statues of forgotten saints stand among patches of dead grass.

The church dominates the skyline, its weathered stone darkened by age, while shattered stained-glass windows reflect the last traces of daylight in fractured colors. Even from this distance, the scent of rot grows stronger, and every instinct tells you that the hunt is almost over.

You tighten your grip on your weapon and continue toward the entrance.


[move Church]


:: Defeat {"position":"1400,600","size":"100,100"}
Your strength fails before the monster does. The final blow tears through your guard, and the cold stone rushes up to meet you. 

As your vision fades, the creature's ragged breathing is the last sound you hear before darkness claims Dravenhold once more.

[close]


:: EnemyTurn {"position":"1200,600","size":"100,100"}
